# General to this entire file, not just this block: a .chezmoiremove entry is a standing
# declaration, not a one-shot cleanup. chezmoi re-deletes the destination path on every
# future `chezmoi apply`, so if a user or another tool ever puts a file back at one of
# these paths, it vanishes again on the next apply with no warning. (~/.claude/skills and
# ~/.codex/skills are both symlinks to ~/.agents/skills, verified on disk, so a single
# `.agents/skills/<name>` entry here removes the path for both harnesses at once — and a
# skill authored from either harness lands on that same shared path.)
#
# agent-browser specialized skills. The CLI serves these at runtime via
# `agent-browser skills get <name>` (version-matched, never stale), so vendoring the
# static SKILL.md is redundant. Only the discovery stub (dot_agents/skills/agent-browser)
# stays managed; these previously-deployed copies are removed.
# #145 (2026-06-12) removed all five skills from source in one commit, but .chezmoiremove
# did not exist yet, so nothing was registered for any of them. #174 (2026-06-22)
# re-curated electron/slack/dogfood, and #175 (2026-06-23) re-removed those same three
# and registered only them here. agentcore and vercel-sandbox were never re-curated after
# #145, so neither commit had a removal target for them, and their already-deployed
# copies lingered unregistered until this PR.
.agents/skills/electron
.agents/skills/slack
.agents/skills/dogfood
.agents/skills/agentcore
.agents/skills/vercel-sandbox

